    <div class="report-container">
        <!-- Header -->
        <div class="header">
            <h1>Student Performance Analytics Report</h1>
            <div class="subtitle">Factors Influencing Academic Outcomes in Bangladesh</div>
            <div class="meta">
                <div>Report Generated: April 29, 2026</div>
                <div>Dataset: 1,000 students across 8 districts</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Table of Contents -->
        <div class="toc">
            <h3>Table of Contents</h3>
            <ol>
                <li><a href="#executive-summary">Executive Summary</a></li>
                <li><a href="#demographic">Student Demographic Overview</a></li>
                <li><a href="#academic">Academic Performance Analysis</a></li>
                <li><a href="#socioeconomic">Socio-Economic Factors and Their Impact</a></li>
                <li><a href="#study-behavior">Study Behavior and Attendance Patterns</a></li>
                <li><a href="#regional">Regional Performance Disparities</a></li>
                <li><a href="#recommendations">Key Findings and Policy Recommendations</a></li>
            </ol>
        </div>

        <!-- Executive Summary with KPIs -->
        <div class="section" id="executive-summary">
            <h2>Executive Summary: Key Performance Indicators</h2>

            <div class="highlight-box">
                <strong>Primary Finding:</strong> The average HSC Result across Bangladesh is 4.01 (on a 0-5 scale), with 26.8% of students achieving Excellent performance (GPA ≥ 4.5). Notably, 0% of students fall into the At-Risk category (GPA < 3.0), suggesting a baseline competency threshold is being met across all districts. However, the near-zero correlation between socio-economic factors and outcomes warrants further investigation.
            </div>

            <div class="kpi-grid">
                <div class="kpi-card">
