                    <div class="kpi-value">0.0%</div>
                    <div class="kpi-label">
                        <span class="kpi-indicator" style="background: var(--success)"></span>
                        At-Risk Student Rate
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="kpi-card warning">
                    <div class="kpi-value">+0.018</div>
                    <div class="kpi-label">
                        <span class="kpi-indicator" style="background: var(--accent)"></span>
                        GPA Progression Delta
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="kpi-card">
                    <div class="kpi-value">-0.014</div>
                    <div class="kpi-label">
                        <span class="kpi-indicator" style="background: var(--text-muted)"></span>
                        Attendance-Performance Correlation
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h3>Key Observations</h3>
            <ul style="margin-left: 20px; margin-top: 15px;">
                <li><strong>Minimal Socio-Economic Impact:</strong> Contrary to expectations, family income, parent education, and internet access show negligible correlation with HSC outcomes (all |r| < 0.02). This suggests other factors may be more determinative of student success.</li>
                <li><strong>GPA Progression:</strong> Students show a slight overall improvement from Previous GPA to HSC Result (+0.018), with 50.7% improving and 48.4% declining. Students with lower previous GPAs are most likely to improve (86.5% of low performers improve).</li>
                <li><strong>Regional Variation:</strong> Barisal and Rajshahi lead with average HSC results above 4.09, while Rangpur trails at 3.91 — a 0.20 GPA point gap warranting targeted intervention.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 1: Demographic Overview -->
        <div class="section" id="demographic">
            <h2>1. Student Demographic Overview</h2>

            <p>This section summarizes the composition of the student population across key demographic dimensions.</p>

